The "runables" folder has all the player-usable things. The instructions .txt has a link to the web version, and instructions for the linux version. My devlogs can be found in logs.txt, some early concept ideas in ideas.txt, and the code in project.py

I intend to add more cards, enemies, and a longer story in future weeks, so this is just the start, and serves as more of an engine-demo than a final game, but I hope it's fun.

A text-based deckbuilding game, inspired by slay the spire and Inscryption, produced in python. 
Some card names and jokes are taken from various media I watch, such as the gravity falls episode "Dungeons, Dungeons, and more Dungeons".

To run on linux, simply download the file, then run it in terminal. It should not need elevated permissions from something like sudo. 
It may need chmod +x so it can run
It must be run in terminal, as it otherwise has nowhere to print to or take input from. If you have python, you can just download and run the .py in the main folder

A web build can be found here -> https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1tOv6YmSUzfUQCbn6S9GJeMMKIg2i1Y5D?usp=sharing
The web build will likely suffer a little in speed and quality due to being run in google colab, but I had no other way to make it web-runnable.
